  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 300 AM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nSaturday...Current ensemble handling the ridge periphery and short \nwave timing suggest that most of Sat may be a lull window in the \nconvective onslaught. This may allow for a full on warm front \nretreat back north bathing most of the cWA in a steamy warm sector \nwith highs in the upper 80s or near 90 with high sfc DPTs well up in \nthe 70s. If this scenario holds, Saturday may be a candidate for the \nneed of a heat headline. Then the nocturnal processes kick in for \nmore storm chances Sat night.\n\nSunday through Thursday...Medium range ensembles suggest an upper \npattern flux with brunt of the upper ridge retrograde and some \nflattening and trending of the mid CONUS steering flow to a \nnorthwesterly regime by early next week. This process may come at \nthe risk of shunting a cool font down through the area late Saturday \nnight or Sunday with an associated storm risk, but eventually lead \nto a cooler and more settled weather regime for at least Monday into \nTuesday. But even west-northwesterlies usher acrs short waves and \nMCV's and we may be due again for some convection by mid next\nweek.",
